//23// //24// Having thus stated the proof for his own thesis, he presents the proof for the opponent's thesis concerning the ground of dispute and refutes it.
"Now, of sound" —
Since deviation is obtained through intangible (<s>asparśa</s>) action alone on both sides, the raising of the deviation through eternal atoms is to be seen as for the purpose of refuting co-extensiveness (<s>samavyāptikatva</s>), just as [in the case of] the impermanence of what is produced. //22-24//

